And for his son, from Sparta, of Alector he was leading home the daughter —
who, late-born, to him was born, the mighty Megapenthes,
by a slave-woman;

So they were feasting throughout the high-roofed great house,
neighbors and kinsmen of Menelaus, glorious,
taking their delight;

But the two, again, in the forecourt of the house, themselves and their two horses,
both the hero Telemachus and Nestor's splendid son,
brought to a stand;

And hand-water a handmaid poured over them, bringing it in a pitcher,
a fine golden one, over a silver basin,
for washing;

but then, afterward,
having tasted of the meal, the two of you, we shall ask who you are
of men;

for surely for you two, at least, the stock of your parents has not perished,
but of men you are the stock, of Zeus-nurtured kings,
scepter-holding, since not base men could beget such as you.”

for indeed, having suffered much and having wandered much,
I brought it home in my ships, and in the eighth year I came,
to Cyprus and Phoenicia and the Egyptians having wandered,

While I, around those lands, much livelihood gathering together,
was wandering, meanwhile another man my brother slew,
secretly, unlooked-for, by the guile of his accursed wife;
